e band immediately below, 11.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.2, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.8 to 6.3. Contract [1], for 14,907.45 euros, was awarded in October 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: a pile-up of amounts just under the limit is a statistical indicator. It does not prove that any contract was broken up or that anyone acted improperly; it may reflect market prices, fixed budgets or separate needs.\nWhat can be checked: in the linked contract files, what was bought in each case and on which dates, and whether several contracts meet a single need that could have been procured at once.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"plantilla","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["eP0eTZdEF2Zq1DdmE7eaXg%3D%3D","PvrC4SPAB%2BSS81gZFETWmA%3D%3D","88fjT9W%2BIrktm4eBPtV6eQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}